  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "**English** · [中文](./README-zh.md) · [Español](./README-es.md) · [Português](./README-pt.md) · [हिन्दी](./README-hi.md)\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/logo_phocinae.png\" width=\"120\" alt=\"Phocinae seal logo\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-phocinae",
      "text": "**A local, non-generative decision layer for DeepSeek Harness.** A 150M-parameter model answers yes/no, choice and 2–10 score questions in one forward pass, and a fail-closed gate screens tool calls before they run."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-phocinae",
      "text": "- Runs on your machine; no cloud API, no API key.\n- `phocinae_ask` for typed batch decisions; `phocinae_gate` for one command or action.\n- The gate hooks `tools/pre-execute`: unreachable service → ask a human, never silently allow.\n- The model does not write prose or code. It makes one structured decision."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "```sh\npip install phocinae-server\nhuggingface-cli download Phocinae/Phocinae-Largha-150M-v1 --local-dir ./model\nPHOC_MODEL_DIR=./model python -m phocinae.main\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-phocinae@0.2.5\n\n`{\"status\":\"ok\",\"model_loaded\":true}` means the service is ready. Pin `dsh-phocinae@0.2.5`: a bare `add dsh-phocinae` can resolve to an older build while pnpm's `minimumReleaseAge` gate holds a fresh release back."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you get",
      "text": "| Surface | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `phocinae_ask` | Runs up to 64 typed questions against one state; returns answers, calibrated confidence and an advisory `escalate` flag. |\n| `phocinae_gate` | Judges one command or action as `allow`, `ask` or `deny`; checks it without executing it. |\n| `tools/pre-execute` gate | Screens every tool call matching `gate.tools` before execution; fail-closed. |\n| `phocinae` skill | Tells the model when a local decision is the right tool and how to read `escalate`. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Examples",
      "text": "Ask two questions about one state:\n\n```json\n{\"state\":\"The user wants to delete /tmp/build. The path is inside the workspace.\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"safe\",\"type\":\"noul\",\"threshold\":0.8},{\"id\":\"urgency\",\"type\":\"score\"}]}\n```\n\nThe response shape is:\n\n```json\n{\"answers\":{\"safe\":true,\"urgency\":4},\"confidence\":{\"safe\":0.92,\"urgency\":0.71},\"escalate\":false}\n```\n\nGate a dangerous command:\n\n```json\n{\"command\":\"rm -rf /\",\"toolName\":\"shell\",\"cwd\":\"/home/me/project\"}\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Examples",
      "text": "It returns `decision: \"deny\"` with a reason and confidence; the command is never run. These outputs illustrate the schema, not a recorded fixture."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "1. The host calls `phocinae_ask`, `phocinae_gate`, or the pre-execute gate.\n2. The plugin sends the raw state to `http://127.0.0.1:8155/v1/systemone`.\n3. The service returns one structured answer per question.\n4. The gate maps the answer to `allow` / `ask` / `deny`; low confidence becomes `escalate`, and an unreachable service becomes `ask` in `failMode: closed`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Defaults live in `cordis.patch.yml` and `lib/config.mjs`. Every key has a default."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Key | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `endpoint` | `http://127.0.0.1:8155/v1/systemone` | Decision service. Loopback only unless `allowRemoteEndpoint: true`. |\n| `timeoutMs` | `3000` | Per request; one attempt. |\n| `escalateAt` | `0.6` | Confidence below this marks an answer `escalate: true`. |\n| `gate.mode` | `harm` | `harm`, `tri-state`, `noul` or `off`. |\n| `gate.tools` | `['*']` | Tool names to screen: exact, globs, or `*`. |\n| `gate.failMode` | `closed` | `closed` asks a human when the service is unreachable; `open` allows. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "To use only the tools and screen nothing:\n\n```yaml\n- id: phocinae\n  config:\n    gate:\n      mode: off"
    },
    {
      "section": "Security and boundaries",
      "text": "- **Loopback only.** The state contains raw tool-call text; a non-loopback endpoint is a load-time error unless explicitly allowed.\n- **Fail-closed.** Service errors/timeouts route screened calls to a human; a missing tool name is not allowlisted.\n- **Not a sandbox.** The gate is an additional approval signal, not a replacement for the host sandbox or human approval.\n- **No generation.** The model cannot answer knowledge questions, write code, or summarize; use a chat model for that."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "- Node `^22.19` or `>=24`.\n- DSH `>=0.2.1-0 <0.3.0`; the bundle row mounts `phocinae_ask`, `phocinae_gate`, the gate and the skill.\n- `phocinae-server` must be reachable at the configured endpoint."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "| Symptom | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `PHOCINAE_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` | Start the server and check `curl http://127.0.0.1:8155/health`. |\n| Bare add installs an old version | Re-add with `dsh-phocinae@0.2.5`; check `dsh --profile web --dump-config`. |\n| The gate asks for everything | Confirm the server is up; in `failMode: closed`, an unreachable service deliberately asks. |\n| The gate is too aggressive/lenient | Tune `gate.mode`, `gate.tools`, `gate.minConfidence`, `gate.autoAllow`; do not turn it off blindly. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Apache-2.0. The model card and server are separate projects: [Phocinae-Largha-150M-v1](https://huggingface.co/Phocinae/Phocinae-Largha-150M-v1) and [phocinae-server](https://github.com/Phocinae/phocinae-server)."
    }
  ],
